  "query_preview": "Forecast Discussion...\n\nHeading into next week, we'll see a short relaxation of the flow \naloft, but a progressive flow is expected to resume.  Signal \nanalysis suggests a signal crossing around 12/3-12/4 with another \nsignal crossing around 12/7-12/8.  The teleconnection pattern \nsuggests that the AO will become slightly negative along with the \nNAO becoming more negative with time.  The PNA pattern had a fairly \nstrong positive signal a few days ago, but has trended weaker in the \nlast several model runs.  EPO forecast call for a strong +EPO \npattern as we head into the month of December.  A look at the \nhemispheric flow shows a strong area of lower surface pressures \nsettling east of the Urals next week.  If this verifies, we'll be \nlooking at a negative mountain torque and we should see the Pacific \njet slowdown and retract a bit to the west.  The Euro has been \ncapturing this quite well over the last few runs and the retraction \nwould lead to more considerable troughing over the western CONUS \nalong with downstream ridging across the eastern US.  This leads us \nto believe that a milder pattern will hold sway in early December \nwith a continued progressive pattern aloft bringing additional \nweather systems across the region yielding higher than normal \nprecipitation chances.",
